# RushDay API, first pass (stage S2): index, health, public status and the session flow.
# Start the API with scripts/run-api.ps1 (never dotnet run). Every non-GET request needs the X-CSRF-TOKEN header,
# whose value arrives in JSON only: from /api/auth/csrf before signing in, from the login response after.
# Stage S11 completes this file with the student, lecturer and administrator journeys.

@RushDay_HostAddress = http://localhost:5080

### JSON index (story, links)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api

### Liveness (Render's health check)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/health/live

### Readiness (database check, rate-limited per address)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/health/ready

### Public status (demo accounts only when Demo:Enabled)
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/public/status

### 1. Anonymous antiforgery token (sets the rushday.csrf cookie)
# @name csrf
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/csrf

### 2. Sign in as the demo student
# @name login
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{
  "username": "S000001",
  "password": "Student-Demo-2026!"
}

### 3. Who am I (a fresh token for the signed-in identity)
# @name me
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me

### 4. A mutation without the header is refused: 400 urn:rushday:antiforgery
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout

### 5. Sign out (rotates the security stamp: every session of the account ends)
POST {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{me.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Unknown API route: JSON 404, never index.html
GET {{RushDay_HostAddress}}/api/nope
